# Out of the Hollow Mouth at dawn, then the walk up the south trail to Highbank (scripts/mouth_escape.gd).
# Claude's draft lines for Preston, 2026-10-11 (Preston: the partner should explain the courier side, that it
# wants into the Wayline and needs a partner, so the theft at the Job Board makes sense). Proposals, edit freely.
# Same rules as flood_bank.dialogue: "Name: line" is spoken, a bare line is narration, [#face] picks the
# portrait, "- " lines are choices. "do walk_on()" moves the two of you a stretch further up the trail.
# How we write: docs/design/dialogue-voice-guide.md.

~ start
You come up out of the dark into gray morning light. The rain has quit.
{{partner_name}}: [#surprised] ...Huh. Would you look at that. The sun actually came up.
{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] We made it! We actually made it out of there!
Behind you the ruin sits high and dry on its stones, like it's been there forever. The river has gone down to a sulk.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] That thing was not there yesterday. I've walked this bank my whole life.
- What was that place?
	{{partner_name}}: [#worried] A Hollow. Folks call 'em that, the holes that open up in the river. Nobody's real sure where they come from.
	{{partner_name}}: [#worried] Things live down there. Things that don't much care for company. You saw.
- Is the parcel okay?
	{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] Dry as a bone. Don't ask me how, but I'm not complaining.
{{partner_name}}: [#determined] C'mon. Highbank's up the south trail. Walk with me, I'll fill you in on the way.
do walk_on()
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] So. Highbank sits way up on the bluff, so the water never gets it. Every town on this river leans on it.
{{partner_name}}: Down here the roads wash out every spring. Only way anything gets anywhere is if somebody carries it.
{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] That's the Wayline. Couriers. Runners, we call 'em. Mail, medicine, seed, whatever needs going, a runner takes it. Through a Hollow if they have to.
do walk_on()
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] The Wayline Hall's right in the middle of town. Starward runs it. The Postmaster.
- You want to be a runner.
	{{partner_name}}: [#sad] ...Is it that obvious? Yeah. Since I was little.
- So you're a runner?
	{{partner_name}}: [#sad] Not yet. Trainee. Been one a good while, too.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] Starward's got one rule that won't budge. Nobody runs a route alone. You run with a partner or you don't run.
{{partner_name}}: [#sad] And every runner's already paired up. Nobody wants the trainee who's never carried a thing.
do walk_on()
{{partner_name}}: [#determined] But this right here is Wayline mail I pulled out of a flood. If I walk it through that door myself, they gotta take me serious.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] ...Only I'd need a partner standing next to me when I do it.
{{partner_name}} goes quiet for a few steps.
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] I mean. You did follow me through a whole Hollow without running off. That's more than most.
- I'll be your partner.
	{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] For real? You're not just saying that? ...Okay. Okay! Partners!
- Let's see how it goes.
	{{partner_name}}: [#happy] That's fair. That's fair. I'll grow on you.
do walk_on()
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] One thing, though. Up there, keep an eye on this parcel. Not everybody who carries mail carries it honest.
{{partner_name}}: [#angry] There's a bunch that call themselves the Shortcut Crew. They'll take a job right out of your hands and sell it back to you.
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] But hey. What are the odds, right?
The trail climbs. Up ahead, Highbank's roofs catch the first of the sun.
=> END
